From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:25:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/31] Keep agent hooks inside their own Git work tree

muse -w creates a linked worktree inside the repository
(<repo>/.muse/worktrees/<date>-<hex>), so a hook there walked up into
the main work tree's .dmc/ and recorded the turn in the wrong vault.
dmc agent-hook now records nothing, and warns on stderr, when the
nearest .git marker above its cwd sits below the .dmc root: a linked
worktree, a nested repository or a submodule. It uses marker positions
only, with no git process, and still exits 0 with empty stdout. Each
worktree gets its own vault and checkpoints after dmc init there.

status and doctor show whether the workspace is a linked worktree and
its main work tree, or, for a main work tree, its linked worktrees and
which have a vault. They read Git's metadata files; no git process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
